/-!
# transferAndCall: the conditions of the paths and the names of their ends

Generated by `scripts/gen_defs.py` from the terms of the generated paths; do not edit.

The arguments of the call (`tacTo`, `tacValue`, `tacOff`, `tacLen`, `tacData`) and the numbers of
the length (`tacN`, `tacW`, `tacF`) are in Args.lean. Here:

- the conditions of the branches, as the words the code tests (`TacToZero`, `TacToSelf`,
  `TacLow`, `TacOver`, `TacHasCode`, and the other side of each);
- the gas of each path (`tacDoneGas`, `tacCallGas`), the memory at the CALL (`tacMem`), the data
  of the two logs (`tacLog1Data`, `tacLog2Data`) and the call data (`tacCallData`);
- `tacDoneSs_eq`, `tacCallSs_eq`: the substate at the two ends, with both logs in view.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.deprecated false
set_option maxRecDepth 8192

namespace LinkVerify.Tac

open UsdtVerify
open TokenKit
